.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-184/tmp/production-source10c136-139-review/source-first.md-4-
.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-184/tmp/production-source10c136-139-review/source-first.md-5-2026-11-17; STEMROBIN-184; human-authorized offline sidecar. Stage A ONLY. Zero author disclosure. Only original 10c physical pages 136-139 and up to four registered new minimal native glyph crops are eligible pixel evidence. No author artifact, sourcepage.md, page.json, review, answer key, choice output, old history, TOC, app, DB, Git, web, API, workflow, publisher, finalize, assemble, render, or test was consulted or operated.
.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-184/tmp/production-source10c136-139-review/source-first.md-6-
.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-184/tmp/production-source10c136-139-review/source-first.md:7:All paths, byte hashes, native pixel hashes, dimensions, mode, DPI, equality checks and permanent load events are in sibling ledger.md. Original coordinates below are rough native-pixel XYWH, top-left origin, not machine-snapped boxes. They identify observed objects and visually read printed rows, not mechanical bands, masks, exclusions, expected-count edits, or production instructions.
.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-184/tmp/production-source10c136-139-review/source-first.md-8-
.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-184/tmp/production-source10c136-139-review/source-first.md:9:`Rnn` denotes one actual printed horizontal text row. Multiple text objects sharing a horizontal row get one R identifier. A numerator and denominator in one typeset fraction are not extra rows. Figure ink, including labels inside the figure, is inventoried separately and is not counted as prose rows. Figure captions, teaching footnotes, headings and footers ARE text rows. Unicode is used deliberately for faithful Chinese transcription and visible mathematical/typographic distinctions. Math is encoded with LaTeX, without resolving conflicts by algebra. Rough punctuation spacing is typographic, not an inferred new row.
.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-184/tmp/production-source10c136-139-review/source-first.md-10-
.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-184/tmp/production-source10c136-139-review/source-first.md-11-Semantic object IDs and ownership here are independently observed local labels, not authoritative published IDs. No unsolved exercise is invented from a proof, historical discussion, worked example, or theorem.
